    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (77.12) and **Yordan Alvarez** (75.72) anchoring the offense. **Junior Caminero** is our strongest play, bolstered by a significant 16% park factor advantage and a favorable matchup against Trevor Rogers, while **Yordan Alvarez** continues to operate in elite territory with a massive .460 xwOBA against J.T. Ginn. Furthermore, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.54) and **Trea Turner** (67.61) provide critical stolen base upside; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** specifically benefits from a 14% platoon boost against Emerson Hancock, making him an essential component of our pursuit of league-leading SB efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the final OF spots and the bench. **Christian Yelich** (39.41) barely remains in the active lineup despite a difficult matchup against Chris Sale, as our depth remains thin at the position. **Carson Benge** (47.96) was the most prominent exclusion from the starting nine; while he boasted a higher daily efficiency score than **Christian Yelich**, the optimizer favored maintaining **Christian Yelich**'s veteran floor over the combined risk of **Carson Benge**\u2019s SP skill disadvantage and a 37% rain risk in his contest. Elsewhere, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (65.08) is a high-upside start against Freddy Peralta, as his 16% park boost and the likelihood of base-stealing opportunities against a slow-delivering pitcher make him a superior play to the more conservative options on our bench, such as **Gary Sanchez** (39.77) or **Josh Smith** (42.99). We will be monitoring the pending lineups closely, as any shift from our assumed batting orders\u2014particularly for **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith**\u2014could recalibrate these daily scores given their heavy reliance on order-based production metrics.",
